  // RULE 14 - A CANONICAL CTA CARRYING A PROCLITIC.
  // Ruled by Hussein 2026-09-08, on the corrected touch sent the same day: the model
  // wrote \u0644 + \u0623\u062a\u0645 ..., which reads as a first-person "so that I complete
  // the purchase" rather than the canonical phrase. The failure is structural, not
  // stylistic: APPROVED_CTA is MASKED OUT above before any marker runs, so a letter
  // welded onto the front of a CTA destroyed the evidence of itself and passed every
  // rule. The masking is right - \u0623\u0643\u0645\u0644 alone is still an informal imperative
  // everywhere else - so the prefix has to be caught BEFORE the mask, against `body`.
  //
  // Only prefixes that change PERSON or MOOD are rejected: \u0644 (li-, subjunctive),
  // \u0633 (sa-, future) and \u0628 (bi-). \u0648 and \u0641 are deliberately allowed - they are
  // plain conjunctions that leave the verb untouched, and rejecting them would degrade
  // ordinary sentences for nothing. Widen the list if a real message proves otherwise.
  const CTA_PROCLITICS = ['\u0644', '\u0633', '\u0628'];
